learnings:
  - 'The loop closure converged on the loader, not the orchestrator: hooking settlement inside updateTask means completeTask/shelveTask/direct-set all trigger it with zero drift — the single-chokepoint insight from Loid''s rev.2.'
  - 'Falsifiability achieved by instrumenting the PIPE not the OUTPUT: chainLive (every non-skipped stage ok, written in finally) distinguishes a clean silence-is-signal run (chainLive:true, 0 journals) from a severed chain (chainLive:false) — the circular JPS metric could not. A reviewer can sever postflight and watch paradigm doctor flip red.'
  - 'Belief-delta promotion was correctly NOT shipped: confidence_before is a fabricated branch literal, so a real prior needs unbuilt elicitation + corpus migration. v7.0 ships honest absolute-confidence with a real confidence_after; belief-delta is v7.x. Shipping the delta on synthetic numbers would have been the exact ''asserted not true'' failure v7 exists to kill.'
